From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:02:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: pin CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib for the vendored
 mbedTLS/libdatachannel builds

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [manylinux-image-specific build layout, not relevant upstream]

CMakeLists.txt's own target_link_libraries() calls hardcode
${LIBDATACHANNEL_INSTALL_DIR}/lib/libdatachannel.a (and the libjuice/
libsrtp2/libusrsctp/mbedtls .a files alongside it), but the
ExternalProject_Add() calls that build those dependencies never pin
CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR, so each sub-build's own CMakeLists.txt (via
GNUInstallDirs) picks whatever that image's multiarch heuristic
decides. On manylinux's Rocky Linux 10 base that is lib64 for a 64-bit
target, not lib, so the install step ships
install/lib64/libdatachannel.a while the final link step still looks
in install/lib/, and ld fails with "cannot find
.../install/lib/libdatachannel.a: No such file or directory" for every
one of the seven vendored .a files. Upstream's own CI never hits this:
its `build_ubuntu` job (which this port's workflow is explicitly based
on) runs on Ubuntu, where GNUInstallDirs' heuristic picks lib even for
a 64-bit target. Pin CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib on both ExternalProject
builds so the install path matches what the parent CMakeLists.txt
already assumes, rather than widening every hardcoded lib/ path to
lib64/ or auditing which image family the next contributor builds on.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index a119a49..d565971 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -131,6 +131,7 @@ else()
         -S ${MBEDTLS_SOURCE_DIR}
         -B ${MBEDTLS_BUILD_DIR}
         -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=${MBEDTLS_INSTALL_DIR}
+        -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib
         -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
         -DENABLE_TESTING=OFF
         -DENABLE_PROGRAMS=OFF
@@ -177,6 +178,7 @@ else()
     DOWNLOAD_EXTRACT_TIMESTAMP TRUE
     CMAKE_ARGS
       -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=${LIBDATACHANNEL_INSTALL_DIR}
+      -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib
       -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
       -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF
       -DUSE_MBEDTLS=ON
--
2.43.0

